You can use the `ExceptionUtils` class from the Apache Commons Lang library to get the stack trace of an exception. Here's an example:

```java
import org.apache.commons.lang3.exception.ExceptionUtils;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            // Code that might throw an exception
            int x = 1 / 0;
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            // Get the stack trace
            String stackTrace = ExceptionUtils.getStackTrace(e);
            System.out.println(stackTrace);
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, we're catching an `ArithmeticException` and then using `ExceptionUtils.getStackTrace(e)` to get the stack trace of the exception. The stack trace is then printed to the console.

